    "body": "I work on confidential projects, where the thought of accidentally pushing to a GitHub remote is horrifying.\r\n\r\nAs a safety measure I have defined local versions of wflow_git_remote() and wflow_git_push() that call stop(\"Don't do that!). However, that doesn't prevent some function calling workflowr::wflow_git_push().\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to add a local_only=TRUE argument to wflow_start() that takes steps to ensure that workflowr never tries to have dealings with a remote repo?",
